$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure D: In a screw cap tube, bromopyrazole (1 equiv.),
phenylboronic acid (1.2 equiv.), Pd(dtbpf)Cl2 (0.1 equiv.) and K2CO3 (1.5
equiv.), were added in acetonitrile/water (1/1, 0.1 M). The reaction
mixture was stirred at 100 °C overnight, then filtered on celite and
washed with ethyl acetate. The filtrate was then washed with brine. The
organic layer were collected, dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate and
evaporated under vacuum. The crude mixture was purified by column
chromatography. •
1-(4-methylphenyl)-5-phenyl-4-(2-phenylethyl)-1H-pyrazole (6a) Compound
6a was obtained with 41 mg, 75% yield (bright yellow solid) from 3b (55
mg, 0.16 mmol) and phenylboronic acid (24 mg, 0.20 mmol) using general
procedure D and purified by column chromatography (Heptane/Ethyl acetate:
95/05). Mp: 119-121 °C 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400MHz): δ = 7.61 (s, 1 H),
7.32-7.05 (m, 14 H), 2.89-2.77 (m, 4 H), 2.31 (s, 3 H) ppm; 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 101MHz): δ = 141.6, 139.9, 139.8, 137.8, 136.5, 130.7, 129.9
(2C), 129.2 (2C), 128.5 (2C), 128.4 (2C), 128.3 (2C), 128.0, 125.9, 124.4
(2C), 120.7, 31.1, 26.0, 21.0 ppm; IR (ν, cm-1): 3027, 2921, 2857, 1604,
1516, 1496, 1444, 1454, 1384, 1090, 1071, 964, 819, 772, 697, 659, 583,
551, 515; MS (ESI) m/z: 339 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
