$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 7. Synthesis of Compounds 7 and 8. A mixture
of iodobenzene (0.025 mL, 0.222, 2.5 equiv), oxaborole 3a or 3k (0.089
mmol, 1 equiv), K3PO4 (25.8 mg, 0.121 mmol, 1.5 equiv), toluene-H2O (0.5
mL – 0.1 mL) and Pd(PPh3)4 (18.7 mg, 0.016 mmol, 0.2 equiv) was stirred
at 100 °C for 6 h under Ar. At the end of the reaction, the mixture was
cooled and extracted with toluene. The organic layer was washed with
brine and dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was purified by column chromatography over silica using an
hexane/ethyl acetate 7:3 as the eluent. The 7 or 8.
(3E,4E)-3-(Benzo[d]oxazol-2-yl(phenyl)methylene)-4,5-diphenylpent-4-en-2-ol
(8): 28.2 mg, 71 %. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.52-7.58 (m, 1H, HAr),
7.28-7.41 (m, 8H, HAr), 7.06-7.24 (m, 6H, HAr), 6.96-7.04 (m, 2H, HAr),
6.91 (s, Ph-C=CH-Ph), 6.73-6.78 (m, 2H, CHAr), 4.64 (q, J=6.6 Hz, 1H,
CH-O), 1.49 (d, J=6.6 Hz, 3H, CH3-CH O) ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ
163.5 (N-C-S), 150.5 (C-O), 148.7 (C=C CHOH), 148.1 (C-N), 143.2 (CAr),
141.8 (CAr), 139.0 (CAr), 137.5 (Ph-C=CH-Ph), 129.6 (2CHAr), 129.3
(2CHAr), 128.7 (2CHAr), 128.4 (2CHAr), 128.3 (2CHAr), 128.2 (CHAr), 128.0
(CHAr), 127.8 (2CHAr), 127.7 (CHAr), 127.4 (Het-C=C), 125.0 (Ph CH=C-Ph),
124.1 (CHAr), 122.8 (CHAr), 120.2 (CH-C-N), 110.5 (CH-C-O), 68.6 (CH OH),
22.8 (CH-CH3) ppm. IR (CH2Cl2) ν 3320, 2989, 2931, 1741, 1587 cm-1. Anal.
Calcd. for C31H25NO2: C, 83.95; H, 5.68. Found: C, 83.93, H, 5.70.
